{"name":"Onyx","hex":"#464544","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Onyx","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Kern County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Onyx"}],"entries":[{"title":"Onyx","blocks":[{"text":"Onyx is a typically black-and-white banded variety of agate, a silicate mineral. The bands can also be monochromatic with alternating light and dark bands. Sardonyx is a variety with red to brown bands alternated with black or white bands. The name \"onyx\" is also frequently used for level-banded (parallel-banded) agates, but in proper usage it refers to color pattern not band structure. Onyx, as a descriptive term, has also been incorrectly applied to parallel-banded varieties of alabaster, marble, calcite, obsidian, and opal, and misleadingly to materials with contorted banding, such as \"cave onyx\" and \"Mexican onyx\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Agate-Quartz-49959.jpg/330px-Agate-Quartz-49959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Onyx","wikidata":"Q180884"},{"title":"Onyx (hip-hop group)","blocks":[{"text":"Onyx is an American hardcore hip hop group from New York City, formed in 1988 by Fredro Starr, Suavé and the late Big DS. Sticky Fingaz joined the group in 1991."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/59/Onyx_%28hip_hop_group%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Onyx_(hip-hop_group)","wikidata":"Q936693"},{"title":"Shades of black","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of black, or off-black colors, are colors that differ only slightly from pure black. These colors have a low lightness. From a photometric point of view, a color which differs slightly from black always has low relative luminance. Colors often considered \"shades of black\" include onyx, black olive, charcoal, and jet."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cc/Color_icon_black_new2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_black","wikidata":"Q7460340"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Red_onyx_-_Handicraft.jpg/500px-Red_onyx_-_Handicraft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Red_onyx_-_Handicraft.jpg/500px-Red_onyx_-_Handicraft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cabochons of red onyx, also called sardonyx","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_onyx_-_Handicraft.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Black_Onyx.jpg/250px-Black_Onyx.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/14/Black_Onyx.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Black_Onyx.jpg/250px-Black_Onyx.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black onyx with white streaks","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Onyx.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Kunsthistorisches_Museum_Vienna_June_2006_031.jpg/500px-Kunsthistorisches_Museum_Vienna_June_2006_031.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Kunsthistorisches_Museum_Vienna_June_2006_031.jpg/1280px-Kunsthistorisches_Museum_Vienna_June_2006_031.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Kunsthistorisches_Museum_Vienna_Jun